!   line 40  (no location, no binary)             -   CALLING SEQUENCE ** LVI,1,DEN CODE    (0 - HIGH, 1.0 - LOW)
!   line 41  (no location, no binary)             -                        SIC,K DEN OK<sep>B,K K DENS
!   line 42  (no location, no binary)             -
!   line 43  221466.00   000000.61 8B 001027.20 50   K K DENS L(BU,1),S U DENS($11),46   -TEST IF UNIT SET TO DESIRED DEN
!   line 44  221467.00   000011.02 90             KV,1,$R
!   line 45  221467.40   221474.72 C2             BXE,K DEN OK
!   line 46  221470.00   221471.74 C2             BRZ,K LOW                  -IF NOT SEE WHATS DESIRED
!   line 47  221470.40   000036.05 01             LVI,2,(8)36.               -HIGH DENSITY DESIRED
!   line 48  221471.00   221472.10 00             B,$+1.0
!   line 49  221471.40   000037.05 01    K LOW    LVI,2,(8)37.               -LOW DENSITY DESIRED
!   line 50  221472.00   000000.61 8B 001000.30 F0            CM1100(BU,1),S U DENS($11)   -SET UNIT DENSITY BIT IN UST
!   line 51  221473.00   221475.00 10             LX,0,K CTL CM
!   line 52  221473.40   221502.00 80             SIC,K SEOP R
!   line 53  221474.00   221476.10 00             B,K K EOP
!
! Lines 1-3 and 36-42 print a "-" in the NAME column and NOTHING in
! the LOCATION and BINARY OUTPUT columns, so there is nothing for a
! !CHECK to test and they are not in the deck.  All forty-three
! located rows ARE checked below.
!

!SYM KRWEF   221444.40
!SYM RK2     221464.00
!SYM KSOSTM  221465.00
!SYM KKDENS  221466.00
!SYM KLOW    221471.40
!
!CHECK 221444.40 | 000036.05 02 | line 4 K R WEF LCI,2,K REP -- the LCI immediate occupies the address field's WORD part only; measured, every bit offset from .00 to .77 on the operand prints the same 000036, so this row pins K REP to WORD 30 and no further. .05 is 2J+1 = 5 for J=2, the same field the five LVI rows print
!CHECK 221445.00 | 000136.05 01 | line 5 LVI,2,(8)136. -REWIND TAPE -- a LITERAL, so this row is a pure encoding check with no symbol in it: 0o136 is Reference Manual p.132's Rewind control code and the operator's comment says so in English. Byte 01 against line 4's 02 is the only difference between LVI and LCI
!CHECK 221445.40 | 221475.00 10 | line 6 LX,0,K CTL CM -- HALF WORD ONLY: measured, an LX prints .00 for every operand offset 0-31 and .40 for 32-63, so this row establishes K CTL CM is in the LOW half of word 221475 and nothing finer. THIS ROW CARRIES THE FIRST LOCATION-COLUMN ASTERISK. Lines 24 and 51 are the identical card without one
!CHECK 221446.00 | 221502.00 80 | line 7 SIC,K SEOP R -- AN SIC CARRIES ITS OPERAND'S FULL 24-BIT BIT ADDRESS (workflow), so K SEOP R is read at 221502.00 BIT-EXACT. Line 52 is the same card and prints the same half word, which is this page's own control on the reading
!CHECK 221446.40 | 221476.10 00 | line 8 B,K K EOP -- target+.10; bit offset unobservable, and only bit 32 is checked. Line 53 is the same card
!CHECK 221447.00 | 221325.40 80 | line 9 SIC,K UNR R -- SIC, so BIT-EXACT at 221325.40; printed p.184 line 22 is the SAME CARD and prints the same half word, and its deck landed K UNR R at that address independently
!CHECK 221447.40 | 221321.50 00 | line 10 B,K K LOOP -WAIT FOR END OP REW -- 0o40 OR 0o10 = 0o50 on K K LOOP's landed 221321.40, so this checks the half word; printed p.184 line 23 prints the identical word
!CHECK 221450.00 | 221313.40 80 | line 11 SIC,K CBJ R -- SIC, so BIT-EXACT at 221313.40; printed p.184 line 24 is the same card and agrees
!CHECK 221450.40 | 221302.50 00 | line 12 B,K CLEAR -CLEAR CONTROL WORD -- 0o40 OR 0o10 = 0o50 on K CLEAR's landed 221302.40; printed p.184 line 25 prints the identical word
!CHECK 221451.00 | 000000.03 01 | line 13 LVI,1,S INST D -SET UNIT TO INSTALLATION DENS -- .03 is 2J+1 = 3 for J=1 with bit 32 CLEAR, so S INST D is in word 0's low half; printed p.108's defining card gives 0.0 exactly and its dds (BU,24) is carried here so the merged image cannot disagree
!CHECK 221451.40 | 221474.40 80 | line 14 SIC,K DEN OK -- SIC, so K DEN OK is read at 221474.40 BIT-EXACT. This address is ONE HALF WORD PAST THIS PAGE'S LAST ROW, which is why the deck predicts it is printed p.191's line 1. Line 21 is the same card and agrees
!CHECK 221452.00 | 221466.10 00 | line 15 B,K K DENS -- K K DENS is THIS page's line 43 at 221466.00, so this is a real address check and not a tautology: 0o00 OR 0o10 = 0o10. Line 22 repeats it
!CHECK 221452.40 | 000021.00 80 221730.06 A0 | line 16 TI,3,$1,J PREV X -- the first address is $1's own cell, word 0o21 = 17 (index registers occupy words 16-31), which is a pure encoding check with no symbol. The second is J PREV X: measured, a TI's second operand prints .06 for every offset 0-31 and .46 for 32-63, so this is HALF WORD ONLY
!CHECK 221453.40 | 221660.00 80 | line 17 SIC,J WRIT X -- SIC, so J WRIT X is read at 221660.00 BIT-EXACT. Nothing else on this page or in any landed deck names it, so this row is its only witness
!CHECK 221454.00 | 221644.50 00 | line 18 B,J R WRIT -ERASE LONG GAP + REWRITE LABEL -- 0o40 OR 0o10 = 0o50, so J R WRIT is at 221644.40 to the half word; the typeset C22-6728/6678 print JRWRIT four times, which is what settles the spelling and not the address
!CHECK 221454.40 | 000002.33 8D 001027.20 50 | line 19 L(BU,1),S F DEN($13),46 -SET UNIT TO FILE DENSITY -- A VFL OPERAND IS THE FULL 24-BIT BIT ADDRESS, so S F DEN is read at 000002.33 = word 2 bit 0o33 = 27 BIT-EXACT, and printed p.102 line 12's defining card gives 2.27. 8D's low nibble is index $13; the second word is the (BU,1) dds 0o001027 with the offset 46 in IBM bits 44-50 and the L code 20 50
!CHECK 221455.40 | 000011.02 30 | line 20 LV,1,$R -- the operand is $R, word 0o11 = 9, the right half of the accumulator, so this is an encoding check with no symbol: .02 is 2J = 2 for J=1, the even-J counterpart of line 13's 2J+1. The printed fraction field reads ".C2" on the page and a C cannot occur in an octal field, so it is .02 (workflow rung 5)
!CHECK 221456.00 | 221474.40 80 | line 21 SIC,K DEN OK -- the second of three readings of K DEN OK on this page; identical to line 14, which is what makes either one trustworthy
!CHECK 221456.40 | 221466.10 00 | line 22 B,K K DENS -- the second branch to this page's own line 43; identical to line 15
!CHECK 221457.00 | 000117.05 01 | line 23 LVI,2,(8)117. -RETRY WEF OP -- a LITERAL. 0o117 is Reference Manual p.132's Write Tape Mark, and the comment calls it the WEF op, which is the name-to-code join strap_asm's IO_FUNCTION_OPS note is missing for WEF
!CHECK 221457.40 | 221475.00 10 | line 24 LX,0,K CTL CM -- identical to line 6 and WITHOUT the asterisk line 6 carries, which is the measurement that kills "the asterisk marks this mnemonic"
!CHECK 221460.00 | 221512.40 80 | line 25 SIC,K K RET -- SIC, so K K RET is read at 221512.40 BIT-EXACT; this row is its only witness anywhere
!CHECK 221460.40 | 221505.10 00 | line 26 B,K IO REJ -- 0o00 OR 0o10 on K IO REJ's 221505.00, HALF WORD only. The printed hex byte reads "CO" on this page and a branch byte here is 00; the octal field two characters away is clean, so this is the per-CHARACTER ink dropout the workflow warns about, not a different byte
!CHECK 221461.00 | 221462.03 01 | line 27 LVI,1,$+1.0 -- $ is this row's own 221461.00, so $+1.0 is 221462.00 and .03 is 2J+1 = 3 for J=1 with bit 32 clear. THE ROW IS SELF-CHECKING: it depends on nothing but this page's counter, and it carries the SECOND location-column asterisk
!CHECK 221461.40 | 221525.10 00 | line 28 B,J SEOP T -CHECK TERMINATION -- HALF WORD only on 221525.00. The spelling is settled in TYPESET prose: JSEOPT 5 hits against JSECPT 1 in C22-6728/6678
!CHECK 221462.00 | 221465.10 00 | line 29 B,K SOS TM -EPGK - GIVE UP AFTER 3 TRIES -- K SOS TM is THIS page's line 34 at 221465.00, a real internal address check. EPGK is indicator 9 and the comment is naming the condition, not an operand
!CHECK 221462.40 | 221464.10 00 | line 30 B,RK2 -- RK2 is THIS page's line 33 at 221464.00, internal
!CHECK 221463.00 | 221274.10 00 | line 31 B,K SOS -EE - VERY SHORT TAPE -- 0o00 OR 0o10 on K SOS's 221274.00, landed by printed p.125 from an OCR'd defining card. EE is indicator 11
!CHECK 221463.40 | 221422.50 00 | line 32 B,K K EXIT -SUCCESSFUL END -- 0o40 OR 0o10 = 0o50, so K K EXIT is at 221422.40 to the half word; nothing else names it
!CHECK 221464.00 | 000011.77 80 221274.34 00 | line 33 RK2 BZB,$R.63,K SOS -- the first address is $R bit 63: word 0o11 = 9 and bit 0o77 = 63, so the system-symbol-plus-bit form is checked outright with no external in it. The second is K SOS, and measured, a BZB's target prints .34 for every offset 0-31 and .74 for 32-63, so it is HALF WORD ONLY and agrees with the landed .0
!CHECK 221465.00 | 221445.04 48 | line 34 K SOS TM CB,2,K R WEF.32 -- SUBSTITUTED AS KRWEF.32, see ONE SUBSTITUTION; the value is unchanged. K R WEF is THIS page's line 4 at 221444.40 and .32 is BARE DECIMAL (workflow), so +32 bits is 221445.00 and .04 is 2J = 4 for J=2. The row is therefore an internal address check of this page's own first label
!CHECK 221465.40 | 221274.10 00 | line 35 B,K SOS -- identical to line 31, the two being each other's control
!CHECK 221466.00 | 000000.61 8B 001027.20 50 | line 43 K K DENS L(BU,1),S U DENS($11),46 -TEST IF UNIT SET TO DESIRED DEN -- A VFL OPERAND IS BIT-EXACT: S U DENS is read at word 0 bit 0o61 = 49, matching its landed SYN(BU,1), 0.49. 8B is index $11; the second word is the identical dds/offset/opcode group as line 19, which differs only in the index and the first address -- the two rows are each other's control on the L encoding
!CHECK 221467.00 | 000011.02 90 | line 44 KV,1,$R -- the same $R cell and the same 2J = 2 field as line 20, with the KV byte 90 against LV's 30. THE PAIR IS WHAT IDENTIFIES THE MNEMONIC: two rows one page apart, same operand, same printed address, different byte
!CHECK 221467.40 | 221474.72 C2 | line 45 BXE,K DEN OK -- a branch on indicator XE (53): 0o40 OR 0o32 = 0o72, where 0o32 = 26 = 53>>1 is the indicator field. So this row checks K DEN OK's HALF WORD a third time and the indicator outright. printed p.184 line 5's BZXE prints the same 0o32 with bit 32 clear and byte C0, the branch-if-OFF form
!CHECK 221470.00 | 221471.74 C2 | line 46 BRZ,K LOW -IF NOT SEE WHATS DESIRED -- a branch on indicator RZ (57): 0o40 OR 0o34 = 0o74, and 0o34 = 28 = 57>>1. K LOW is THIS page's line 49 at 221471.40, so the address half is an internal check
!CHECK 221470.40 | 000036.05 01 | line 47 LVI,2,(8)36. -HIGH DENSITY DESIRED -- a LITERAL: 0o36 is Reference Manual p.132's High Density Mode, with the operator's English beside it. The same .05 field as lines 5 and 23
!CHECK 221471.00 | 221472.10 00 | line 48 B,$+1.0 -- $ is 221471.00 so the target is 221472.00; self-checking, and NOTE IT CARRIES NO ASTERISK although line 27's $+1.0 does
!CHECK 221471.40 | 000037.05 01 | line 49 K LOW LVI,2,(8)37. -LOW DENSITY DESIRED -- 0o37 is p.132's Low Density Mode. This row's own English is what settles the label's round glyph: the comment prints LOW and the name prints LOW
!CHECK 221472.00 | 000000.61 8B 001000.30 F0 | line 50 CM1100(BU,1),S U DENS($11) -SET UNIT DENSITY BIT IN UST -- the SAME first address and index as line 43 through a different operation, so S U DENS at word 0 bit 49 is read twice on this page; the second word is the bare (BU,1) dds 0o001000 with offset 0 and the CM1100 code 30 F0
!CHECK 221473.00 | 221475.00 10 | line 51 LX,0,K CTL CM -- the third printing of this card; identical to lines 6 and 24
!CHECK 221473.40 | 221502.00 80 | line 52 SIC,K SEOP R -- the second BIT-EXACT reading of K SEOP R; identical to line 7
!CHECK 221474.00 | 221476.10 00 | line 53 B,K K EOP -- identical to line 8, and the last located row on the page. The counter leaves this page at 221474.40
